From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] smsutil: take cell broadcast topics up to 9999

The Topics property of org.ofono.CellBroadcast took 0 to 999, and
cbs_optimize_ranges() had a bitmap of as many bits. Every public warning
identifier is above that: ETWS starts at 4352, CMAS and EU-Alert at 4370.
So voicecall's channel catalog, which sets them, gets "Argument format is
not recognized" for a whole set of topics, and a phone subscribes to no
warning at all. On the Mindphone that is the state of both modems.

The EFcbmi and EFcbmir reads had the same limit, so warning identifiers a
SIM asks for were dropped as well.

Sailfish made this change in 93352582. Here the bitmap stays on the stack:
1250 bytes is no burden. The loop counter in cbs_optimize_ranges() is an
unsigned short, so the limit cannot go past 65534 without changing that.

"1-5, 3333" in the invalid ranges of test-sms is now valid, so 10000 takes
its place, and the new test checks what comes out, not only that something
does.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/src/cbs.c b/src/cbs.c
index 8113673..843710e 100644
--- a/src/cbs.c
+++ b/src/cbs.c
@@ -704,7 +704,7 @@ static void sim_cbmi_read_cb(int ok, int length, int record,
 
 		mi = (data[i] << 8) + data[i+1];
 
-		if (mi > 999)
+		if (mi > CBS_MAX_TOPIC)
 			continue;
 
 		range = g_new0(struct cbs_topic_range, 1);
@@ -751,7 +751,7 @@ static void sim_cbmir_read_cb(int ok, int length, int record,
 		min = (data[i] << 8) + data[i+1];
 		max = (data[i+2] << 8) + data[i+3];
 
-		if (min > 999 || max > 999 || min > max)
+		if (min > CBS_MAX_TOPIC || max > CBS_MAX_TOPIC || min > max)
 			continue;
 
 		range = g_new0(struct cbs_topic_range, 1);
diff --git a/src/smsutil.c b/src/smsutil.c
index 84895c4..7bf6a5e 100644
--- a/src/smsutil.c
+++ b/src/smsutil.c
@@ -4451,7 +4451,7 @@ out:
 GSList *cbs_optimize_ranges(GSList *ranges)
 {
 	struct cbs_topic_range *range;
-	unsigned char bitmap[125];
+	unsigned char bitmap[CBS_MAX_TOPIC / 8 + 1];
 	GSList *l;
 	unsigned short i;
 	GSList *ret = NULL;
@@ -4471,7 +4471,7 @@ GSList *cbs_optimize_ranges(GSList *ranges)
 
 	range = NULL;
 
-	for (i = 0; i <= 999; i++) {
+	for (i = 0; i <= CBS_MAX_TOPIC; i++) {
 		int byte_offset = i / 8;
 		int bit = i % 8;
 
@@ -4511,10 +4511,10 @@ GSList *cbs_extract_topic_ranges(const char *ranges)
 	GSList *tmp;
 
 	while (next_range(ranges, &offset, &min, &max) == TRUE) {
-		if (min < 0 || min > 999)
+		if (min < 0 || min > CBS_MAX_TOPIC)
 			return NULL;
 
-		if (max < 0 || max > 999)
+		if (max < 0 || max > CBS_MAX_TOPIC)
 			return NULL;
 
 		if (max < min)
diff --git a/src/smsutil.h b/src/smsutil.h
index 2c1c7d2..e622b5f 100644
--- a/src/smsutil.h
+++ b/src/smsutil.h
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 enum cbs_language;
 
 #define CBS_MAX_GSM_CHARS 93
